# WarpOne formal proof (Phase 4 + Phase 5) via yosys's built-in SAT temporal induction.
# Properties live in rtl/core/warpone_core.v under `ifdef FORMAL`:
#   - per-warp mask-stack safety: sp <= DEPTH always (no silent over/underflow corruption)
#   - scheduler no-deadlock: while running with a live warp, the core issues or releases
# Assumption: reset asserted in the initial state ($initstate) so registers are defined.
# We use yosys `sat` (minisat) rather than smtbmc+z3 because the local z3 4.8.12 hangs on
# this model at step 0 (solver pathology); see DECISIONS D5.2. Run from the repo root.
read_verilog -sv -formal -DFORMAL -I rtl/core rtl/core/warpone_core.v
prep -top warpone_core
memory_map
opt -full
# -tempinduct: unbounded proof by temporal (k-)induction; -verify: nonzero exit on failure.
sat -tempinduct -prove-asserts -set-assumes -seq 20 -verify
